    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d455">

                <pb facs="0506" n="1184" sameAs="frus:frus1863p2/pg1184"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Morris</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 51.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-02-02"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >February</hi> 2, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the pleasure to enclose herewith a
                    transcript of a letter of the 20th ultimo, addressed to this department by the
                    secretary of the American Board of Commissioners for Foreign Missions at Boston,
                    on the subject of your successful exertions to bring to punishment the assassins
                    of the Rev. Mr. Merriam.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>E. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Joy Morris</hi>, Esq., <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c., Constantinople.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
